# Fires whenever sys.boot.reason becomes any non-empty value. Bootstat
# sets it during boot — early via the `on post-fs && property:ro.boot.bootreason`
# action in bootstat.rc when ro.boot.bootreason is non-empty, and later
# refined via `bootstat --set_system_boot_reason` at
# ro.persistent_properties.ready=true. By using a property trigger we run
# AFTER the value is populated; using `on post-fs-data` runs *before*,
# while sys.boot.reason is still empty.
#
# The binary itself short-circuits cheaply on non-panic values, so it's
# safe to fire on every transition.
on property:sys.boot.reason=*
    exec - root root -- /system/bin/panic_to_recovery
